# CLAUDE.md — user instructions (template)

User-scope memory (`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — loads in every project on this
machine, distinct from a project's own `CLAUDE.md`). This template carries
only the rules that are genuinely portable across machines; sections that
name specific facts about one machine or one set of personal repos are
deliberately left out or marked for per-machine fill-in. Copy this file to
`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` on a new machine and adapt the marked sections — do not
sync it verbatim between machines afterward, since the Environment section
below is fill-in-per-machine by design.

Portability audit (why each section is here, or isn't) is documented in the
shenlong-skills repo's session history — see the split rationale in this
repo's own root `CLAUDE.md` under "shenlong-skills plugin" for context on why
this repo is the source of truth across machines in the first place.

## Response style

Adjust freely per user preference — nothing machine-specific here. Example
from the source machine: a caveman-mode plugin injects a marker on every
prompt, honored for the whole session with normal prose kept for code,
commit messages, PR descriptions, security warnings, and confirmations of
irreversible actions.

